{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>העירותי.</b> The he is pathach because of the ayin that follows it." "<b>מצפון.</b> For Elam is north-east of Babylon, and the word איש is lacking, so it is as though: העירותי איש מצפון, and he is Cyrus." "<b>ויאת.</b> A strange word, because the peh and the lamed are quiescent letters, and it ought to have been on the pattern of ויפן. And when the alef disappeared, they widened what precedes it according to the rule of guttural letters; therefore the yod is in pathach, and it is of the binyan qal." "<b>ויבא [סגנים].</b> In the lands of satraps, or in the camp of satraps, and he tramples them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:28.363380549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}